  "stemOverrides": {
    "1": "Position of an ant (\\(S\\) in metres) moving in \\(Y - Z\\) plane is given by \\(S = 2t^{2}\\widehat{j} + 5\\widehat{k}\\) (where \\(t\\) is in second). The magnitude and direction of velocity of the ant at \\(t = 1\\text{ }s\\) will be:",
    "12": "A rectangular loop of length \\(2.5\\text{ }m\\) and width \\(2\\text{ }m\\) is placed at \\(60^{\\circ}\\) to a magnetic field of \\(4\\text{ }T\\). The loop is removed from the field in \\(10sec\\). The average emf induced in the loop during this time is",
    "14": "A convex lens of focal length \\(40\\text{ }cm\\) forms an image of an extended source of light on a photoelectric cell. A current I is produced. The lens is replaced by another convex lens having the same diameter but focal length 20 cm (leading digit dropped; exact value NOT recoverable from the booklet). The photoelectric current now is:",
    "15": "A body of mass \\(1000\\text{ }kg\\) is moving horizontally with a velocity \\(6\\text{ }m/s\\). If \\(200\\text{ }kg\\) extra mass is added, the final velocity (in \\(m/s\\) ) is:",
    "21": "A particle starts from origin at \\(t= 0\\) with a velocity \\(5\\widehat{i}m/s\\) and moves in \\(x - y\\) plane under action of a force which produces a constant acceleration of \\((3\\widehat{i}+ 2\\widehat{j})m/s^{2}\\). If the \\(x\\)-coordinate of the particle at that instant is \\(84\\text{ }m\\), then the speed of the particle at this time is \\(\\sqrt{\\alpha}m/s\\). The value of \\(\\alpha\\) is ________ .",
    "22": "A thin metallic wire having cross sectional area of \\(10^{- 4}{\\text{ }m}^{2}\\) is used to make a ring of radius 30 cm. A positive charge of \\(2\\pi C\\) is uniformly distributed over the ring, while another positive charge of 30 \\(pC\\) is kept at the centre of the ring. The tension in the ring is _____ \\(N\\); provided that the ring does not get deformed (neglect the influence of gravity). (given, \\(\\frac{1}{4\\pi\\epsilon_{0}}= 9 \\times10^{9}\\) SI units)",
    "24": "Two immiscible liquids of refractive indices \\(\\frac{8}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) respectively are put in a beaker as shown in the figure. The height of each column is 6 cm. A coin is placed at the bottom of the beaker. For near normal vision, the apparent depth of the coin is \\(\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\text{ }cm\\). The value of \\(\\alpha\\) is \\(\\ \\) .",
    "26": "Four particles each of mass \\(1\\text{ }kg\\) are placed at four corners of a square of side 2 m. Moment of inertia of system about an axis perpendicular to its plane and passing through one of its vertex is ___ \\(kgm^{2}\\).",
    "27": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion with an amplitude of 4 cm. At the mean position, velocity of the particle is 10 cm/s. The distance of the particle from the mean position when its speed becomes \\(5\\text{ }cm/s\\) is \\(\\sqrt{\\alpha}cm\\), where \\(\\alpha =\\) ________ .",
    "28": "Two long, straight wires carry equal currents in opposite directions as shown in figure. The separation between the wires is 5.0 cm. The magnitude of the magnetic field at a point \\(P\\) midway between the wires is ______ \\(\\mu T\\) (Given: \\(\\mu_{0}= 4\\pi \\times10^{- 7}TmA^{- 1}\\) )",
    "29": "The charge accumulated on the capacitor connected in the following circuit is _____ \\(\\mu C\\) (Given C = 150 microF)",
    "100": "The total kinetic energy of 1 mole of oxygen at \\(27^{\\circ}C\\) is: [Use universal gas constant (R) = 8.31 J/mole K]",
    "110": "A bullet is fired into a fixed target looses one third of its velocity after travelling 4 cm. It penetrates further \\(D \\times10^{- 3}\\text{ }m\\) before coming to rest. The value of \\(D\\) is:",
    "111": "The magnetic field at the centre of a wire loop formed by two semicircular wires of radii \\(R_{1}= 2\\pi m\\) and \\(R_{2}= 4\\pi m\\) carrying current \\(I = 4\\text{ }A\\) as per figure given below is alpha x 10^-7 T. The value of alpha is ___ __________ . (Centre \\(O\\) is common for all segments)",
    "113": "A closed organ pipe \\(150\\text{ }cm\\) long gives 7 beats per second with an open organ pipe of length 350 cm, both vibrating in fundamental mode. The velocity of sound is ______ \\(m/s\\).",
    "114": "A body falling under gravity covers two points A and B separated by 80 m in 2 s. The distance of upper point \\(A\\) from the starting point is _____ \\(m\\) (use \\(g = 10{\\text{ }ms}^{- 2}\\) )",
    "115": "The reading of pressure metre attached with a closed pipe is \\(4.5 \\times10^{4}\\text{ }N/m^{2}\\). On opening the valve, water starts flowing and the reading of pressure metre falls to \\(2.0 \\times10^{4}\\text{ }N/m^{2}\\). The velocity of water is found to be \\(\\sqrt{V}m/s\\). The value of \\(V\\) is _____",
    "117": "A parallel beam of monochromatic light of wavelength \\(5000\\text{Å}\\) is incident normally on a single narrow slit of width 0.001 mm. The light is focused by convex lens on screen, placed on its focal plane. The first minima will be formed for the angle of diffraction of _____(degree)."
  },
